{"topic": "4.3 Conversion and Conservation of Energy", "level": "b8", "lessons": [{"subject": "sci", "level": "b8", "topic": "4.3 Conversion and Conservation of Energy", "kind": "learn", "title": "Energy Conversion and Conservation in Daily Life", "emoji": "\ud83c\udf1f", "order": 1, "status": "draft", "pages": [{"title": "What you will learn", "body": "\ud83c\udfaf **By the end of this lesson you will be able to:**\n- Classify the importance of energy conversion and energy conservation in daily life.\n- Search from multimedia sources, books and the internet for information on the impact of energy conversion and conservation on the environment.\n- Make a poster presentation on findings about energy conversion and conservation in the environment."}, {"title": "Energy Conservation Explained", "body": "Energy conservation refers to the practice of reducing unnecessary energy use and avoiding waste, so that a given amount of energy achieves as much useful work as possible. This is different from the law of conservation of energy studied earlier in this strand, which is a scientific principle stating that energy cannot be created or destroyed. Energy conservation, in the everyday sense used in this lesson, is a deliberate human choice and behaviour aimed at using energy wisely."}], "questions": [], "source": "B8_4.1_to_4.5_Forces_and_Energy.docx", "segId": 8}, {"subject": "sci", "level": "b8", "topic": "4.3 Conversion and Conservation of Energy", "kind": "learn", "title": "Importance of Energy Conversion and Conservation in Daily Life", "emoji": "\ud83d\udd2c", "order": 2, "status": "draft", "pages": [{"title": "Importance of Energy Conversion and Conservation in Daily Life", "body": "Reducing costs, extending the life of energy resources, and reducing environmental harm are three broad reasons why energy conversion and conservation matter in daily life. Efficient energy conversion, such as using appliances that convert more of their input energy into useful output rather than wasted heat, directly lowers electricity bills for households and businesses. Conserving energy, such as switching off unused appliances, extends how long limited resources, especially nonrenewable ones, remain available for future use. Both practices also reduce the environmental harm associated with generating additional energy, such as air pollution from burning extra fuel."}, {"title": "Practical Ways to Conserve Energy in Daily Life", "body": "Switching off unused devices, using energy saving bulbs, walking short distances, insulating buildings, servicing machines, and using natural daylight are six simple, practical habits that support energy conservation, as summarised in the table below.\n\n| **PRACTICE** | **HOW IT CONSERVES ENERGY** |\n|---|---|\n| **Switching off lights and appliances when not in use** | Prevents electrical energy from being wasted when no one needs it |\n| **Using energy saving bulbs** | Converts a greater share of electrical energy into light rather than wasted heat |\n| **Walking or cycling for short distances** | Reduces the amount of fuel energy converted into kinetic energy unnecessarily |\n| **Properly insulating buildings** | Reduces the amount of heat energy lost to the surroundings, lowering the energy needed for heating or cooling |\n| **Servicing vehicles and machines regularly** | Keeps engines running efficiently, reducing the energy wasted as excess heat or friction |\n| **Using natural daylight where possible** | Reduces the need to convert electrical energy into light during the day |"}], "questions": [], "source": "B8_4.1_to_4.5_Forces_and_Energy.docx", "segId": 8}, {"subject": "sci", "level": "b8", "topic": "4.3 Conversion and Conservation of Energy", "kind": "learn", "title": "Impact of Energy Conversion and Conservation on the Environment", "emoji": "\ud83e\uddea", "order": 3, "status": "draft", "pages": [{"title": "Impact of Energy Conversion and Conservation on the Environment", "body": "Reduced air pollution, slower depletion of natural resources, and reduced greenhouse gas emissions are three major environmental benefits linked to careful energy conversion and conservation. Since a large amount of the world's energy still comes from burning nonrenewable fuels, any reduction in unnecessary energy use directly reduces the amount of fuel burnt, and therefore the amount of pollutants and greenhouse gases, such as carbon (IV) oxide, released into the atmosphere. This connects directly to the carbon cycle studied earlier in this book, since excessive burning of fuels disrupts the natural balance of that cycle."}, {"title": "Look at the picture", "body": "[[img:i87cb2e4e1|Fig 4.1  Efficient energy conversion, converting as much input energy as possible into a useful output, is central to energy conservation]]\n\nNotice that energy conservation is closely linked to energy conversion, since choosing devices and practices that convert energy efficiently, with less waste as unwanted heat or sound, is itself a form of conserving energy."}, {"title": "Going further", "body": "> \ud83d\udca1 **Going further**\n\nMany governments and organisations now run public awareness campaigns encouraging energy conservation, sometimes called energy efficiency campaigns, which include practical tips such as unplugging chargers when not in use and setting air conditioners to reasonable temperatures. These campaigns recognise that even small individual actions, when adopted widely across a whole community or country, can add up to a significant reduction in total energy use and environmental impact."}], "questions": [{"t": "mcq", "q": "Energy conservation, in the everyday sense used in this lesson, mainly refers to", "o": ["Creating new energy from nothing", "Destroying unwanted energy completely", "Reducing unnecessary energy use and avoiding waste", "Storing all energy permanently without ever using it"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Which of the following is a benefit of energy conservation?", "o": ["Guaranteed higher electricity bills", "Increased air pollution", "Increased waste of resources", "Reduced costs for households and businesses"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Switching off unused appliances mainly helps to", "o": ["Increase unnecessary electricity use", "Make appliances more expensive", "Prevent energy from being wasted", "Reduce the appliance's lifespan"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Using energy saving bulbs mainly helps because they", "o": ["Convert more electrical energy into light rather than wasted heat", "Convert no electrical energy into light at all", "Only work with solar panels", "Use more electricity than ordinary bulbs"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Properly insulating a building mainly helps to", "o": ["Increase heat loss to the surroundings", "Prevent any energy from entering the building", "Reduce heat loss, lowering the energy needed for heating or cooling", "Remove the need for any energy at all"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Which of the following best describes a major environmental benefit of energy conservation?", "o": ["Guaranteed faster resource depletion", "Increased greenhouse gas emissions", "No change to the environment at all", "Reduced greenhouse gas emissions from burning less fuel"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Energy conservation is linked to the carbon cycle because", "o": ["Burning less fuel reduces extra carbon (IV) oxide released into the air", "Energy conservation has no connection to carbon at all", "It only affects electricity, not the atmosphere", "It removes carbon completely from the atmosphere"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Walking or cycling short distances instead of driving mainly helps to", "o": ["Have no effect on energy use", "Increase fuel energy converted into kinetic energy unnecessarily", "Reduce unnecessary fuel energy conversion", "Use more fuel than driving"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Public energy efficiency campaigns are designed mainly to", "o": ["Discourage all use of electricity", "Encourage practical habits that reduce unnecessary energy use", "Increase unnecessary energy waste", "Replace the need for electricity generation entirely"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}, {"t": "mcq", "q": "Which statement best explains why individual actions to conserve energy matter?", "o": ["Individual actions always have zero effect", "Only large industries can make a meaningful difference", "Small actions have no cumulative effect at all", "Small actions, when adopted widely, can add up to a significant overall reduction in energy use"], "c": 0, "e": "", "nokey": true}], "source": "B8_4.1_to_4.5_Forces_and_Energy.docx", "segId": 8}], "images": [{"id": "i87cb2e4e1", "d": "data:image/jpeg;base64,"}], "skippedPics": 0, "skippedQs": {"tf": 0, "syn": 0, "mcqNoKey": 0}}